# Caddy in front of the costing tool, once the server has a domain name. Install as
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile with RIC_HOST set to that name (for example costing.example.uwa.edu.au).
#
# Caddy obtains and renews a Let's Encrypt certificate by itself. Ports 80 and 443 must be
# reachable from the internet for that, and the name must already resolve to this server.

{$RIC_HOST} {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
}
